// EXPECT-ERROR: unterminated string literal
//
// The lexer had always produced this message, but the parser replaced it with
// its own "unexpected token in expression", so no test could see it. parser_error
// now reports the lexer's diagnostic whenever the offending token is a
// TOKEN_ERROR, which is the one path every lexer error takes to the user.
fn main() {
    print("abc)
}
